  "body": "## What changed\n\n**Browser tree (per setup).** The Setup section shows the Setups manager row, then one node per setup. Each node has a radio for the active setup (`ActivateSetup`, undoable) and its own children in the maintainer's order: **WCS, Stock, Machine, Post, Fixtures** (each fixture is a child row), **Tool list, Operations** (1+n, in machining order). A document without setups shows the same children for its implicit setup. The document-wide Operations section is gone. Models and the document's Tools library stay top-level.\n\n**Node pages (right pane).**\n- **Setup row:** opens the setup's settings. These are the active radio, the stock source, part alignment, plane pick, the WCS label (G54-G59) and Delete. The stock source shows \"its own stock\". From the second setup on it also shows a disabled \"the stock <previous setup> leaves behind\" option, which is the hook for #317/#320 and is not implemented here.\n- **WCS:** the origin dialog, plus the setup's G54-G59 label picker.\n- **Stock:** unchanged.\n- **Machine / Post:** a choice between the document's machine/post and the setup's own, then the existing selector.\n- **Fixtures:** load and position this setup's fixtures.\n- **Tool list:** a table of the setup's tools (T number, size, op count, Edit), the number-clash warning, the per-setup tool list and the setup-sheet export.\n- **Operations:** as before.\n\nClicking any node under a setup activates that setup first, in one undoable step. The Stock, WCS, Fixtures, Machine and Post editors work on the active setup, so this way they can never edit a setup the clicked node does not belong to.\n\n**Machine and post per setup.**\n- `SetupDef` gains `machine: Option<MachineDef>` and `post: Option<PostRef>`. `None` (every older file, every new setup) means the setup follows the document's machine/post.\n- New undoable commands `SetSetupMachine` and `SetSetupPost`. They are validated like `LoadMachine` / `SelectPost` and refuse by name.\n- A datum transfer carries the source setup's machine and post.\n- The existing machine and post verbs (ribbon, Stock page, editor) go to the active setup's own machine/post when it has one, and to the document's otherwise.\n- Project version is now **v55**. v54 files open unchanged, and an old build refuses a v55 file.\n\n**The one-mount rule.** The app reads one mounted machine and post, the active setup's (`machine::of`, `kind_of`, `posting::post_of`). Work that would use two different machines or posts is refused by name:\n- generating an op whose setup is on a different machine or post: \"activate 'SetupN' first\";\n- posting a program whose setups use different machines or posts: \"one program is written by one post for one machine\".\n\nWith no setup owning a machine or post, neither refusal can fire, so existing documents generate and post byte-identically.\n\n**Refactor for the 400-line rule.** The browser code moved out of `panes.rs` (2090 → ~1450 lines) into `browser_tree.rs`, `browser_pane.rs` and `tree_menu.rs`. The tree glyphs moved out of `painted.rs` into `tree_glyphs.rs`. The machine/post routing lives in `state_setup_mount.rs`. The new setup pages are in `setup_pages.rs`. `state.rs` gets smaller.\n\n## Decisions (docs/decisions/343-setup-tree.md)\n- **Machine/post per setup is an override.** `None` follows the document, so migration is trivial and posts stay byte-identical.\n- **Posting setups with different posts or machines is refused by name.** Writing one NC file per post is follow-up #388.\n- **Tool list is option (b):** the document library with a per-setup filtered view. The page says that editing a tool edits it in every setup that uses it.\n- **Post options stay document-wide** (follow-up #389).\n- **Clicking a node activates its setup** before its page opens.\n- **Not breaking.** Nothing that loaded before is refused, so there is no `!`.\n\n## Tests\n- `crates/app/tests/setup_mount.rs` (new):\n  - `a_v54_file_follows_the_document_mount_and_posts_byte_identically` (0 and 1 setups)\n  - `a_setups_own_machine_and_post_round_trip_and_undo`\n  - `two_setups_on_different_posts_are_refused_by_name` (post and generation, from both sides)\n  - `two_setups_on_different_machines_are_refused_by_name_and_kinds_follow_the_active`\n  - `the_same_own_post_on_every_setup_posts_like_the_document`\n  - `a_datum_transfer_keeps_the_source_setups_mount`\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/setup_tree.rs` (new):\n  - `every_setup_owns_its_nodes_in_order`\n  - `operations_and_fixtures_sit_under_their_own_setup`\n  - `the_radio_activates_a_setup_undoably`\n  - `each_node_opens_its_page_and_activates_its_setup_first`\n  - `the_machine_and_post_pages_render_for_a_setup`\n  - `machine_and_post_verbs_land_on_the_active_setups_own_mount`\n- Updated: `one_wcs` (one WCS row per setup node), the browser tests in `tests.rs` (ops are now at depth 2; Paste anchors on the setup's Operations row).\n- Shell snapshots regenerated and inspected (`egui_app`, `egui_app_light`, `egui_tool_editor`).\n\n## Gate (worktree, after merging origin/main)\n- **App suites all green:** setups, setup_wcs, one_wcs, posting, per_op_files, project_roundtrip, commands_undo, golden_cl, conformance, machine, setup_sheet, fixtures, setup_mount, turning, setup_align, lathe_post.\n- **ui:** lib 303 passed, `crates/ui --test machine` passed.\n- **clippy:** `-D warnings` clean on app and ui.\n- **Not exercised:** the GUI was not launched by hand.\n\n## Follow-ups\n- #388: generate inactive setups on their own machine; post one file per post.\n- #389: dedicated tool-list export; per-setup post options.\n\nChangelog: The browser shows each setup as a node with an active-setup radio and its own WCS, Stock, Machine, Post, Fixtures, Tool list and Operations; a setup can have its own machine and post (project v55).\n\nFixes #343\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
